From bce80a8a87679d795b3be13137c0dde5339dbc83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Norton <gregory@serenade.local>
Date: Thu, 03 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] WindowServer: Guard AppletManager::set_position against a null window

AppletManager::m_window is created lazily only when applets are added, so it is
null in a session with no applets. The WM-connection destructor calls
set_position({}) unconditionally on every window-manager client disconnect (the
Taskbar is such a client), which dereferenced the null m_window and crashed the
whole WindowServer -- taking down any in-flight screenshot. Guard it like repaint()
already does; with no applet area there is nothing to reposition, so it is a no-op.

diff --git a/Userland/Services/WindowServer/AppletManager.cpp b/Userland/Services/WindowServer/AppletManager.cpp
index 1fb0147a..d84f1e6a 100644
@@ -32,6 +32,8 @@
 
 void AppletManager::set_position(Gfx::IntPoint position)
 {
+    if (!m_window)
+        return; // No applet area yet (no applets added); nothing to reposition.
     m_window->move_to(position);
     m_window->set_visible(true);
 }
